{
  "cases": [
    {
      "i": 4620,
      "title": "Users seeing wrong tenant data and roles not applying",
      "description": "We are experiencing a critical issue in production (LATAM) where a large number of users (approx 16,500) are being redirected to the wrong tenant context upon login. Additionally, their assigned roles are not being applied correctly, resulting in either missing permissions or excessive access. We aren't sure if this is an issue with the SSO handshake itself or if the session data is getting lost/corrupted somewhere in the background message processing. This is blocking operations entirely."
    },
    {
      "i": 4621,
      "title": "SSO sessions expiring prematurely and MFA failures",
      "description": "Starting around 14:00 UTC today, we have noticed that user sessions are timing out after approximately 5 minutes instead of the configured 8 hours. When users are forced to re-authenticate, the MFA codes generated by our provider are being rejected as invalid, even when entered immediately. This is affecting about 50 distinct users in our LATAM production environment. We have verified that the time drift on the MFA token server is <1 second. Please investigate the integration between the SSO module and the MFA validation service."
    },
    {
      "i": 4622,
      "title": "Payment Gateway sessions dropping and MFA rejection",
      "description": "We are observing intermittent session expirations in the Payment Gateway v2 admin console in US-West production. Users are logged out unexpectedly after a few minutes of inactivity, which is below the configured timeout. Furthermore, when attempting to log back in, the 2FA/MFA codes are consistently rejected with an 'Invalid Code' error. This affects roughly 60 users and is causing moderate disruption to our financial operations team. Logs show successful token issuance but subsequent validation failures."
    },
    {
      "i": 4623,
      "title": "Funnel Analyzer displaying incorrect data and 403 errors",
      "description": "In the ANZ production environment, users of the Funnel Analyzer are reporting that the dashboards are loading data from incorrect accounts (cross-contamination). Concurrently, about 15% of the requests to generate these reports are failing with HTTP 403 Forbidden errors. This issue has persisted for the last 24 hours and affects approximately 800 users. We have verified that the user roles and permissions have not changed recently. Please check if there is a caching issue or an authorization service failure."
    },
    {
      "i": 4624,
      "title": "MFA and Login issues in ME Production",
      "description": "Hi, we are having trouble with logins in the Middle East region. Some users can't get the MFA prompt to appear at all. Others are getting locked out because their codes aren't working. It's happening for a few hundred people. Please fix urgently as our sales team is blocked."
    },
    {
      "i": 4625,
      "title": "Vendor Status Page Incident affecting KPI Tracker Sandbox",
      "description": "Our KPI Tracker in the LATAM sandbox environment is currently non-responsive and failing to pull data. We have checked the vendor status page and confirmed there is an active incident listed under 'Data Pipeline Services' starting at 09:30 local time. Approximately 150 users in our development team are affected. We are holding off on our release testing until the vendor resolves the incident, but wanted to log this for internal tracking."
    },
    {
      "i": 4626,
      "title": "Missing MFA prompts for SSO users",
      "description": "We have an issue in EU-Central production. The MFA prompt is not appearing for users when they try to log in via SSO. It just logs them in directly or fails silently. About 500+ users are affected. We are unsure if this is a config drift or a bug. Please advise."
    },
    {
      "i": 4627,
      "title": "Intermittent login failures and MFA rejections on Load Balancer",
      "description": "We are seeing sporadic login failures when users access the application through the Load Balancer in ANZ. The issue manifests as either a generic 'Login Failed' message or an 'MFA Code Invalid' error. These incidents are rare and have not resulted in any support tickets from end-users, but we have detected them in our synthetic monitoring. The load balancer logs show successful SSL terminations, but the backend auth service returns 401s. Since there is no current business impact, this is low priority, but we need to rule out sticky session issues."
    },
    {
      "i": 4628,
      "title": "Database deadlocks during Webhook processing in Dev",
      "description": "In our development environment (ME), we are detecting frequent database deadlocks when the Webhook Engine attempts to write state changes. This is causing webhook deliveries to fail and retry, leading to a backup in the queue. We have isolated the issue to specific transaction types involving user profile updates. This is affecting our ability to test new features and is impacting about 16 developers. Please investigate the locking strategy used by the webhook persistence layer."
    },
    {
      "i": 4629,
      "title": "Identity Vault provisioning stuck and bulk import failures",
      "description": "We are experiencing issues with the Identity Vault in LATAM production. New user provisioning requests are getting stuck in a 'Pending' state and never completing. When we try to bypass this with a bulk import CSV, the process starts but fails partway through with no clear error message. We suspect this might be related to the configuration store not syncing properly with the provisioning engine, or the secret retrieval service is timing out. This affects about 50 new hires and is slowing down onboarding."
    },
    {
      "i": 4630,
      "title": "Payment declined and duplicate charge in Sandbox",
      "description": "In the ANZ sandbox environment for Payment Gateway v2, we encountered a specific test scenario where a transaction was initially declined due to an 'Issuer Unavailable' response, but then successfully processed a duplicate charge immediately after. This occurred with a Visa test card. No other users are affected, and there is no production impact. We are logging this to ensure the idempotency keys are working correctly in the sandbox state."
    },
    {
      "i": 4631,
      "title": "Subscriptions charged twice in APAC Production",
      "description": "We have identified that a significant number of users (approx 450) in the APAC region have been charged twice for their monthly subscription. We are trying to determine if this is a failure in the payment gateway's transaction deduplication logic or if the settlement service is triggering multiple capture requests for a single auth. The customer experience is critical, and we need to understand if the issue lies with the gateway processing or the downstream financial settlement."
    },
    {
      "i": 4632,
      "title": "SSO Account Lockouts and Session Issues",
      "description": "In our APAC production environment, we are seeing a cluster of about 25 users experiencing a loop where their accounts get locked out, they are forced to reset, then their sessions expire immediately, and finally, their MFA codes are rejected. This seems to happen primarily when users switch devices. We have checked the SSO logs and see multiple failed auth attempts followed by successful ones, suggesting a race condition or cache invalidation issue. Please investigate the interaction between session management and the MFA provider."
    },
    {
      "i": 4633,
      "title": "Invoice Service permissions errors and role application failure",
      "description": "Users in the EU-Central production environment who should have 'Viewer' access to the Invoice Service are receiving 'Permission Denied' errors when attempting to access specific reports. Additionally, when we attempt to update roles via the admin console, the changes do not propagate, leaving users with stale permissions. This affects roughly 45 users in our finance department and is causing moderate delays in closing the monthly books. We suspect a synchronization lag between the identity provider and the application's authorization service."
    },
    {
      "i": 4634,
      "title": "Chargeback notices and tax calculation discrepancies",
      "description": "Our finance team in EU-West has flagged several incoming chargeback notices that appear to correspond to transactions that were undercharged. Upon review, the tax amounts applied to these invoices were incorrect (lower than expected), which may have triggered the disputes. We have not seen a direct impact on live transaction processing volume or user experience, so this is currently a data accuracy and compliance issue. We need to audit the tax calculation logic in the Payment Gateway to ensure VAT/GST rules are being applied correctly before these cases escalate."
    }
  ]
